    {'text': 'Custom Solid Wire Contact Pins\nRequest a Quote\nCapabilities Gallery\nSolid Pin Configurator\n800.297.4851\nQUICK LINKS\nAutomotive\nHollow Pins\nSolid Wire Pins\nPin Assemblies\n×\nBuild Your Pins\nCreate solid wire custom contact pins with real-time 3D now\nProduct\n| Custom Solid Wire Contact Pins\nUnlock 30-50% Material Savings with our Precision-Engineered Solid Wire Contact Pins.\nOur unique swaging process ensures precision and value, making Bead the obvious choice when specifying custom contact pins.\nProcesses\nCustomization\nSpecifications\nVideo player - Solid Wire Pins - Click to play video\nProcesses\nBead Electronics offers a versatile range of processes tailored for integrating our wire connector pins into your manufacturing workflow. Each method is designed to accommodate different volumes, automation levels, and cost considerations, ensuring you find the perfect fit for your production needs.\nHand Insertion for Low-Volume Applications\nFor small-scale projects, our custom wire connector pins are available in bulk for manual insertion. This method is ideal for prototypes or low-volume production runs, providing the flexibility to manually fit each connector pin where needed.\nExplore custom connectors and headers suitable for hand insertion here\n.\nBowl Feeding for Automated Assembly', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/products/solid-wire-contact-pins', 'source_title': 'Custom Solid Wire Contact Pins', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 0, 'total_chunks': 4},
    {'text': 'production runs, providing the flexibility to manually fit each connector pin where needed.\nExplore custom connectors and headers suitable for hand insertion here\n.\nBowl Feeding for Automated Assembly\nFor higher efficiency in automated environments, choose our bowl-feeding option. Pins are supplied in bulk, ready to integrate with automated assembly machines, streamlining the orientation and insertion process. This solution is a perfect match for medium to high-volume production that demands speed and consistency.\nLearn more about our bowl feed solution and see it in action here\n.\nTape and Reel for Streamlined Manufacturing\nOur tape and reel packaging offers a balance between upfront costs and long-term manufacturing efficiency. While the initial setup may be higher, this method significantly reduces downstream manufacturing costs, making it a wise choice for large-scale production.\nDiscover the benefits of tape and reel packaging here\n.\nContinuous Reel Insertions for High-Volume Efficiency\nFor the ultimate in efficiency and scalability, our continuous reel insertions provide custom connector pins produced end-to-end on a continuous reel. This method is designed for seamless integration with PCB assembly lines and is compatible with various headers. It offers a streamlined solution for high-volume production, minimizing manual handling and maximizing throughput.\nView our continuous reel options and compatible products here and here\n.\nCustomization', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/products/solid-wire-contact-pins', 'source_title': 'Custom Solid Wire Contact Pins', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 1, 'total_chunks': 4},
    {'text': 't offers a streamlined solution for high-volume production, minimizing manual handling and maximizing throughput.\nView our continuous reel options and compatible products here and here\n.\nCustomization\nWe offer precision-crafted custom solid wire pins with a commitment to quality assurance. Offering complete customization for all our products, our extensive selection includes various configurations, shapes, sizes, and features, suitable for a wide array of applications.\nAutomotive\nAerospace & Defence\nCommunication\nIndustrial\nLighting\nMedical\nSpecifications\nBead Electronics is your go-to for precise and high-quality solid wire pins. These custom connector pins are available in a range of versatile configurations, backed by our exceptional engineering expertise and dedicated customer support. Customers can choose from different base metals and plating options, ensuring a perfect match for specific needs.\nJust ask—all of our products are completely customizable\n.\nSizes\nSquare: 0.012” - 0.062” (0.31mm - 1.90mm)\nLength: .100”-2.000” (2.5-50 mm)\nDiameter: .020”-.312”\nBase Metals\nBrass Alloy\nPhosphor Bronze Alloy\nCopper Alloy 102 and 11\nHigh-Performance Copper Alloys\nStainless Steel\nSteel\nPlating\nTin\nTin/Lead (Not RoHS Compliant)\nNickel\nGold\nPalladium\nSilver\nPackaging\nLoose/Bulk\nTape-N-Reel', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/products/solid-wire-contact-pins', 'source_title': 'Custom Solid Wire Contact Pins', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 2, 'total_chunks': 4},
    {'text': 'osphor Bronze Alloy\nCopper Alloy 102 and 11\nHigh-Performance Copper Alloys\nStainless Steel\nSteel\nPlating\nTin\nTin/Lead (Not RoHS Compliant)\nNickel\nGold\nPalladium\nSilver\nPackaging\nLoose/Bulk\nTape-N-Reel\nThe above list our commonly used specifications but custom productions are always available. Explore our interactive catalog to discover the ideal specifications, features, and configurations that suit your needs.\nRequest a Kit\nReady to take the next step?\nContact us or request a kit to explore our range of hollow pins and find the perfect solution for your project.\nSend Us Your Design\nProducts\nConnector Pins\nCustom Hollow Pins\nCustom Solid Wire Pins\nCustom Pin Assemblies\nMechanical Pins\nOvermolded Pins\nPCB Pins\nIndustries\nAutomotive\nHeavy Equipment\nMilitary & Defense\nCommunication\nIndustrial\nLighting\nMedical\nResources\nBlog\nDownloads\nVideos\nCompany\nAbout Us\nHistory\nOur Team\nCompliance\nCareers\nVirtual Payments\nContact Us\nBead Electronics\n1.800.297.4851\n11 Cascade Blvd.\nMilford, CT 06460\nLocal: 203.301.0270\nToll-free: 1.800.297.4851\nFax: 475.467.6500\nGet In Touch With Us Now\n©\n2026\nBead Electronics All rights reserved |\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nTerms and Conditions', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/products/solid-wire-contact-pins', 'source_title': 'Custom Solid Wire Contact Pins', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 3, 'total_chunks': 4},
    {'text': 'United States Manufacturer | Bead Electronics\nRequest a Quote\nCapabilities Gallery\nSolid Pin Configurator\n800.297.4851\nQUICK LINKS\nAutomotive\nHollow Pins\nSolid Wire Pins\nPin Assemblies\n×\nBuild Your Pins\nCreate solid wire custom contact pins with real-time 3D now\nCompany\n| About Us\nAbout Us\nBead Electronics, a division of\nBead Industries, Inc.\n, specializes in manufacturing custom, high-reliability solid and hollow contact pins and pin assemblies for automotive, datacom, medical, and industrial markets worldwide.\nOur Purpose\nOur purpose is to be a customer-centric company that delivers innovative solutions to our customers, outperforms our competitors and provides a fun and challenging environment for our employees.\nOur Core Values\nAccountability:\nOwn your work\nCollaboration:\nShare your ideas\nResilience:\nPush through obstacles\nExplore & Evolve\nNever stop learning\nOur Team\nJill Mayer\nPresident & CEO\nView Bio\nKristen Moreira\nCFO\nView Bio\nDan Michaud\nVP of Manufacturing\nView Bio\nDavid Brenton\nDirector of Engineering\nView Bio\nDan Tucker\nNew Business Development Manager\nView Bio\nSara Fradette\nCustomer Success & Materials Manager\nView Bio\nRob Stach\nTechnical Sales Manager\nView Bio\nJess Valentino\nQuality & Process Engineering Manager\nView Bio\nTrent Wasserman\nTool & Die Maker / Production Supervisor\nView Bio\nNick Buonaiuto\nMfg Engineer & Equipment Manager\nView Bio\nOur History of Innovation\nTimeline\n1910s\n1920s\n1930s\n1940s\n1950s\n1960s\n1970s\n1980s\n1990s\n2000s\n2010s\n2020s\n1910s', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/company/about-us', 'source_title': 'United States Manufacturer | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 0, 'total_chunks': 4},
    {'text': 'Production Supervisor\nView Bio\nNick Buonaiuto\nMfg Engineer & Equipment Manager\nView Bio\nOur History of Innovation\nTimeline\n1910s\n1920s\n1930s\n1940s\n1950s\n1960s\n1970s\n1980s\n1990s\n2000s\n2010s\n2020s\n1910s\nWaldo Calvin Bryant develops the first electric light pull by using beaded chain. A close friend, Gordon Goodridge, designs the first chain-making machine in America. With Bryant’s son, Gerald, they form the Bead Chain Manufacturing Company, incorporated in March, 1914.\nWaldo Gerald “Gerry” Bryant becomes Bead’s first President.\n1920s\nUtilizing its cold-forming process known as swaging, the company develops radio contact pins. Bead’s\ntubular pin\nsells for half the price of a screw machine part and can be manufactured accurately at high quantities.\n1930s\nThe Navy specifies Bead Chain® aboard ships and on shore, including for use in military ID tags.\n1940s\nDuring WWII, Bead produces more than 22 million Bead Chain® "dog tag" necklace chains for U.S. and Canadian armed forces without a single reject. The company earns the Army-Navy Double EE flag and is given special commendation by the U.S. Ordinance Department.\n1950s\nBead acquires the Bridgeport Silverware Manufacturing Company in 1956, adding plating capacity for its chain and electronics products and leading to the development of the popular "Diamond Jig" fishing lure.\n1960s', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/company/about-us', 'source_title': 'United States Manufacturer | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 1, 'total_chunks': 4},
    {'text': 'the Bridgeport Silverware Manufacturing Company in 1956, adding plating capacity for its chain and electronics products and leading to the development of the popular "Diamond Jig" fishing lure.\n1960s\nBead is at the forefront of developing fluorescent lights. The company manufactures millions of contact pins for fluorescent tubes, supplying parts to GE, Phillips, Sylvania, etc.\n1970s\nBead acquires\nMcGuire Manufacturing Company\nin 1972 and begins marketing high quality, commercial plumbing fixture trim.\nBead Chain® is now available in European markets.\n1980s\nBead changes its name to Bead Industries in 1987 to better reflect its many diverse businesses.\n1990s\nBead Industries develops\nTandem Pins\n® for the printed circuit board industry.\n2000s\nBead moves into a single story, modern facility in Milford, CT, incorporating Lean Manufacturing techniques.\nA partnership with Samwon Petra in South Korea is established to better serve international markets.\n2010s\nBead celebrates its centennial by upgrading to a GF Vertical Milling Center, expanding capabilities and reducing lead time for production tooling by half.\n2020s\nBead achieves IATF certification to support automotive customer needs.\nA prototype of our Next Generation Swaging machines is designed to improve efficiency and capacity.\nProducts\nConnector Pins\nCustom Hollow Pins\nCustom Solid Wire Pins\nCustom Pin Assemblies\nMechanical Pins\nOvermolded Pins\nPCB Pins\nIndustries\nAutomotive\nHeavy Equipment\nMilitary & Defense\nCommunication', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/company/about-us', 'source_title': 'United States Manufacturer | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 2, 'total_chunks': 4},
