    {'text': 'Resources | Bead Electronics\nRequest a Quote\nCapabilities Gallery\nSolid Pin Configurator\n800.297.4851\nQUICK LINKS\nAutomotive\nHollow Pins\nSolid Wire Pins\nPin Assemblies\n×\nBuild Your Pins\nCreate solid wire custom contact pins with real-time 3D now\nResources\n| Downloads\nAccess Helpful Guides, Tip Sheets, eBooks, and more\nAll\nCase Studies\neBooks\nGuides\nVideos\nThe Bead Electronics Swaging Process: From Concept to Reality\nBead’s scrapless swaging process has been minimizing waste while maximizing precision and efficiency since 1914. This unique cold forming process creates consistent components by moving - not removing - metal.\nAre you looking for a custom component supplier who can deliver pins to your specifications? Are you unsure which metal fabrication process would best suit your needs?\nRead More\nReference Guide To Plating For Electronic Connector Pins And Contacts\nChoosing the right plating material for your electrical connectors is critical for ensuring durability, conductivity, and resistance to corrosion.\nNeed a quick reference to decide what plating will best serve your project and budget?\nUnsure which material is ideal for your application?\nRead More\nThe Bead True Grip Pin: An SMT Solution to PCB Pin Insertion\nTrue Grip Pins are a reliable and cost-effective alternative to pin-through-paste processing, which causes debris to be disbursed across the PCB creating contamination, defects, and scrap, as well as bent pins.', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/resources/downloads', 'source_title': 'Resources | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 0, 'total_chunks': 6},
    {'text': "Pins are a reliable and cost-effective alternative to pin-through-paste processing, which causes debris to be disbursed across the PCB creating contamination, defects, and scrap, as well as bent pins.\nBead's True Grip Pin enables you to leverage the through-hole strength while still processing its insertion on the SMT line.\nRead More\nInterconnect Options for Defense and Aerospace Applications\nInterconnection options for defense and aerospace applications are diverse. From boots on the ground to satellites in the sky, there’s a demand for lighter, stronger, and more cost-effective connectors.\nRead More\nCustom Contact Pins for Heavy Duty Applications\nI\nn the heavy equipment and commercial vehicle sector, product integrity and performance are vital for ensuring user safety.\nA standard contact pin may not be sufficient to ensure a reliable connection or hold a signal in harsh environments.\nRead More\nA Complete Contact Pin Customization Guide\nOur complete Customization Guide shows you every component you can customize, including base and plating materials, pin shape, diameter, length, and retention features. Whether you need pins that withstand extreme environments or meet tight tolerances, this guide ensures you have the right information to design contact pins that perform.\nRead More\nA Through Hole Size Guide for Connector Pins", 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/resources/downloads', 'source_title': 'Resources | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 1, 'total_chunks': 6},
    {'text': 't withstand extreme environments or meet tight tolerances, this guide ensures you have the right information to design contact pins that perform.\nRead More\nA Through Hole Size Guide for Connector Pins\nBead Electronics specializes in manufacturing high-quality connector pins, expertly crafted for diverse functionalities such as power, signal transmission, or electro-mechanical uses.\nNeed help determining the right through hole size for your standard connector pins? Look no further. This reference sheet will show you the way.\nRead More\nCustom Contact Pins for PCB Assemblies\nBead Electronics has been manufacturing custom contact pins for PCB assemblies for over a century. Our custom electrical connectors ensure reliable connections even in tough conditions - essential for the automotive, telecom, aerospace, industrial, and medical industries.\nDownload this quick reference guide on our custom pins for PCB applications to discover all the ways Bead can work with you to optimize your contact pin design.\nRead More\nBead Virtual Tour\nBead Electronics is proud to manufacture end to end contact pins, wire contact pins, and hollow contact pins. This video gives you an overview of our Headquarters in Milford, CT.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-virtul-tour - Click to play video\nThe True Grip Pin', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/resources/downloads', 'source_title': 'Resources | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 2, 'total_chunks': 6},
    {'text': ", wire contact pins, and hollow contact pins. This video gives you an overview of our Headquarters in Milford, CT.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-virtul-tour - Click to play video\nThe True Grip Pin\nA feature in our Tandem Pin® series, the True Grip Pin has a square thru-hole section for secure placement into a PCB and a round flange to provide a consistent seating plane giving your solder a large surface for reliable surface mount processing.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-true-grip-pin - Click to play video\nSwaging Process\nThe bead-formed manufacturing process, called swaging, yields superior value. That's because it's a high-speed, virtually scrapless cold-forming process capable of producing small metal parts that are dimensionally consistent and inexpensive.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-swagging-process - Click to play video\nBead Overview\nWatch an overview of our history, our technology, and our latest innovations as a U.S. manufacturer and global leader of precision contact pins.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-overview - Click to play video\n100 Years & Five Generations\nWatch a historical account of Bead over the last 100 years, as told by past and present employees and members of the Bryant family.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-100-years - Click to play video\nCase Study: Custom Pin For Insert Molding\nA well known U.S.-based plastic molder needed a\nright angle pin", 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/resources/downloads', 'source_title': 'Resources | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 3, 'total_chunks': 6},
    {'text': 'embers of the Bryant family.\nVideo player - bead-vid-titleCard-100-years - Click to play video\nCase Study: Custom Pin For Insert Molding\nA well known U.S.-based plastic molder needed a\nright angle pin\nto be insert molded with a leg length longer than any commercially available option. No off-the-shelf solution existed.\nBead Electronics created a custom bend method using a different machine and punch setup to accommodate the length and 90° angle of the pin. Through careful testing, engineers discovered the brass pin required a 2–3° over-bend to achieve a true 90°.\nRead More\nCase Study: Driving Efficiency Through Precision Engineering\nThe customer’s existing blind-rivet design required manual alignment and slow\ninstallation, creating a major production bottleneck.\nBead Electronics engineered a\ncustom square hollow pivot pin\nthat press-fits directly into the extrusion’s semi-circular hole.\nRead More\nCase Study: Reverse Engineering a Critical Connector System\nWhen the customer’s connector system was scheduled to be discontinued, it needed to quickly reverse engineer a replacement to avoid costly redesigns, potential shutdowns, loss of serviceability, increased support costs, and other risks to customer trust.\nBead applied advanced metal-forming expertise to improve manufacturability and consistency while preserving full compatibility.\nRead More\nProducts\nConnector Pins\nCustom Hollow Pins\nCustom Solid Wire Pins\nCustom Pin Assemblies\nMechanical Pins\nOvermolded Pins\nPCB Pins', 'source_url': 'https://www.beadelectronics.com/resources/downloads', 'source_title': 'Resources | Bead Electronics', 'content_type': 'main_site', 'chunk_index': 4, 'total_chunks': 6},
